{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit limit, interest and return rule","requirement":"A landlord may hold no more than one month's rent as a security deposit, must keep it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% interest a year, and return it with an itemized damage list within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent cap; 5% per year interest; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Leases and tenancies of residential real property in Massachusetts; applies to lessors and their agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"A fee in lieu of a security deposit is allowed under executive office regulations if optional and, with any deposit, capped at 1 month's rent in total. Successor liability does not apply to a municipality acquiring title under chapter 60 or to a chartered foreclosing mortgagee.","penalty":"Failure to hold the deposit, give the itemized damage list, or return the deposit within 30 days forfeits the right to retain it and entitles the tenant to three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on amounts collectable at the start of a tenancy","requirement":"At or before the start of a tenancy, a landlord or agent may require no more than first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and the purchase and installation cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"first month + last month rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Any tenancy of residential real property; a lessor or the lessor's agent may not collect amounts above these.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Regulations of the executive office of housing and livable communities may authorize an optional fee in lieu of a security deposit, capped, together with any deposit, at 1 month's rent.","penalty":"A lease term conflicting with the section, or an attempt to obtain a waiver of it, forfeits the lessor's right to retain any portion of the security deposit.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:  (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and,  (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit offer requirement","requirement":"A landlord offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved applicant regardless of income, credit score, race, gender identity, disability, immigration status or household size, and may not use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies where a lessor offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit under regulations of the executive office of housing and livable communities; offered to approved applicants.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.65,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
